  "limitations": [
    "Two reversed-order repetitions of full route rebuilding versus the existing maintained complete route catalog. Both retain checked inventories and fully compose, check plans and select originals.",
    "Each arm pays identical initial session construction and full global query, then at most two batches of twelve advances and 32 entered states per batch, including reentered unfinished states.",
    "Global queries after every batch hold and check the session boundary without resetting the admission ledger. Historical rows, cached objects and complete route objects remain exclusively owned and immutable except for checked acquisition and maintenance.",
    "No persistent negative cache or new route index is added. Restart still reconstructs and checks the full authority. Database and policy guards do not hash arbitrary in-memory mutation.",
    "Full catalog equality audits and authoritative final cold composition are measured separately from matched sequences. Parent replay, reference checking and whole producer time are reported separately.",
    "Two observations on adaptively reused development cases share OS caches; timings are descriptive and object counts are not peak RAM.",
    "No globally minimal expansion, polynomial unrestricted-SAT algorithm or P-versus-NP conclusion."
  ],
